1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,843
Hi, I'm [your name], the solo developer of StubbleTrail, built for the Sustainable Supply Chains track.

2
00:00:07,843 --> 00:00:15,196
StubbleTrail connects agricultural residue to an inspectable evidence trail, from farmer declaration to independent review.

3
00:00:15,196 --> 00:00:25,000
The question behind this project is simple: when a sustainability claim is made, can we examine the records supporting it?

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,875
Consider this synthetic example.

5
00:00:26,875 --> 00:00:33,438
A collector records six hundred kilograms, but the processor receives five hundred and sixty.

6
00:00:33,438 --> 00:00:37,656
Without connected records, the difference is difficult to investigate.

7
00:00:37,656 --> 00:00:41,875
A receipt might also be reused across separate claims.

8
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:50,313
StubbleTrail brings measurements, documents and accountable decisions together, helping reviewers investigate discrepancies before relying on a supply-chain claim.

9
00:00:50,313 --> 00:00:55,000
These examples demonstrate the prototype; they are not field-pilot results.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,800
The workflow has four distinct roles.

11
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:02,000
A farmer registers a plot and declares available residue.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,667
A collector records pickup quantity, measurement basis and event time.

13
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:11,333
A processor independently records intake, the facility and receipt details.

14
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:20,200
Supporting documents are attached to the batch, and an auditor reviews the evidence and findings before recording a decision.

15
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:30,000
In the operational application, permissions are checked on the server; the role selector shown here belongs only to the isolated demo.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,532
AI assists with document reading.

17
00:01:32,532 --> 00:01:41,139
The Gemini integration has been verified using a synthetic PDF, extracting its receipt number and weight correctly.

18
00:01:41,139 --> 00:01:51,266
In the application, the uploader can request structured fields, compare each suggestion with the original document and correct uncertain values.

19
00:01:51,266 --> 00:01:59,873
Confirmation appends a review event; it does not silently replace a custody measurement or approve the batch.

20
00:01:59,873 --> 00:02:06,456
Original files remain private, and extraction requests are subject to database-enforced usage limits.

21
00:02:06,456 --> 00:02:10,000
Human accountability remains part of the process.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,612
StubbleTrail also looks across claims.

23
00:02:12,612 --> 00:02:18,881
Here, two synthetic batches share a receipt identifier and identical file bytes.

24
00:02:18,881 --> 00:02:25,149
The graph makes that relationship visible, while the reviewer documents an explanation.

25
00:02:25,149 --> 00:02:30,373
A match is an investigation signal, not proof of fraud.

26
00:02:30,373 --> 00:02:36,119
SoilSafe adds another question: how much residue is proposed for removal?

27
00:02:36,119 --> 00:02:45,000
It keeps soil cover, nutrients and site-specific review in view, without claiming a universal safe removal threshold.

28
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,671
Each event is linked to the previous event through a canonical SHA-256 hash chain.

29
00:02:52,671 --> 00:03:04,178
Let me demonstrate the integrity check: the recorded chain verifies, but changing a quantity in this copied event produces a mismatch.

30
00:03:04,178 --> 00:03:06,918
The original record remains unchanged.

31
00:03:06,918 --> 00:03:11,301
This makes alterations detectable against the recorded history.

32
00:03:11,301 --> 00:03:25,000
It is not a guarantee against a database administrator rewriting an unanchored chain, which is why the project also supports external commitments on Ethereum Sepolia.

33
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:33,750
The public portal presents a redacted record, custody summary and verification result without exposing private source files or identities.

34
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:39,276
The Solidity registry is deployed on Sepolia with a verified signing authority.

35
00:03:39,276 --> 00:03:44,803
Approved real records can commit their approved event root to that contract.

36
00:03:44,803 --> 00:03:50,789
A confirmed status requires both a successful transaction and a matching registry proof.

37
00:03:50,789 --> 00:03:54,474
This synthetic sample intentionally shows no confirmed anchor.

38
00:03:54,474 --> 00:04:00,000
Blockchain helps verify record integrity; it cannot prove a physical delivery occurred.

39
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:08,000
The prototype is deployed, with Supabase authentication and private storage, Gemini extraction, and the Sepolia registry.

40
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Ninety-three automated unit, API and database tests pass, alongside desktop and mobile workflow tests and local contract checks.

41
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,000
The intended users are cooperatives, residue aggregators and independent reviewers.

42
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Next steps include hosted acceptance testing, organization-scoped access, scalable conflict queries and a documented field pilot.

43
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,000
StubbleTrail aims to make sustainable supply-chain claims easier to examine, without presenting recorded quantities as certified climate benefits.

44
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Thank you.
